-- title:
--   Proper varpi-torsion-free chart ideal is centred at a place
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation domain and $\varpi \in R$ a generator of its maximal ideal, let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field that is both an $R$-algebra and a $K_0$-algebra, compatibly. Let $f \in F$ be non-zero, transcendental over $R$, with $F$ finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(f) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K₀ {f}`. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F f` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $f$, and let `jChartFin R F f` denote $f$ viewed as an element of $A$. Let $I \subseteq A$ be an ideal with $I \ne A$, with $f \in I$, and such that multiplication by the image of $\varpi$ on $A/I$ is injective (any $y$ with $\varpi y = 0$ is zero). The conclusion asserts the existence of a place $v$ of $F$ over $K_0$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_v \subseteq F$ which contains the image of $K_0$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring, such that every element of $A$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_v$ and every element of $I$ lies in the set of non-units of $\mathcal{O}_v$, i.e. in $\mathfrak{m}_v$.
--
--   This is the passage from an ideal of an integral chart algebra to a place of the generic fibre: a proper ideal on which the uniformiser acts without torsion, and which contains the chart coordinate $f$, is dominated by a place of $F/K_0$. It is used in the generic-fibre dictionary for the two-chart integral model, [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_divisor_degree_pos_lSpaceOn_nsmul_le_of_branchData`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_divisor_degree_pos_lSpaceOn_nsmul_le_of_branchData), where such a place carries the branch divisor.
